      "report_date": "2026-11-26",
      "title": "UAC-0218's ForPayload: Document Stealer with Mark Twain quotes targeting Ukraine",
      "summary": "UAC-0218 is using an evolution of the HOMESTEEL malware, dubbed ForPayload, in a campaign running since at least May 2025 against Ukrainian armed forces. The initial sample is a phishing Excel file with a macro that creates a hidden scheduled task, with no third-party malware dropped, running a PowerShell one-liner that uploads recently modified documents, archives and text files to a remote server every week. The malware's comments contain passages from a Mark Twain novel, a technique the researchers note may be meant to hinder analysis heuristics. The actor's infrastructure of more than 50 domains uses Ukrainian, German, and Polish town names, with one domain referencing the Storozhynets city where the 82nd brigade is based. Earlier ForPayload samples from December 2025 use fake OneDrive task names and PE executables, and the researchers link the campaign to UAC-0218 based on similarities to HOMESTEEL.",
      "completeness": "Low",
