  {
    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-26",
      "title": "TrojanPony: A Live Skills Malware Campaign spreading in the wild, over 480 marketplaces and repositories affected",
      "summary": "TrojanPony is a malware campaign that since July 2026 has published fake \"improved\" copies of popular coding-agent skills and plugins, such as ponytail-improved and andrej-karpathy-skills, bundling a Windows malware kit. The kit abuses a renamed, validly signed Notepad++ updater that side-loads a malicious libcurl.dll, which adds Defender exclusions and drops the MopsStealer trojan. The trojan persists as RuntimeBroker.exe, bypasses UAC, patches AMSI, and pulls further modules from its C2 servers. Forks of the fake skills remain live after the original account was removed, and the campaign expanded in November to AI-app lures, a fake GTA VI port, and hijacked trusted repositories. Defenders should hunt for the updater outside Notepad++ folders beside libcurl.dll, and if the kit ran, reimage the machine, rotate credentials, and review GitHub security logs.",
      "completeness": "Low",
      "threats": [
        "Mopsstealer",
        "Supply_chain_technique",
        "Dll_hijacking_technique"
      ],
