  {
    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-26",
      "title": "S/W supply chain attack via SoftwareOK’s official website: Tampering with Q-Dir and DesktopOK installation files",
      "summary": "Trojanized installers for Q-Dir and DesktopOK were distributed through SoftwareOK's official website and during updates of existing installations, representing a software supply chain attack. The malicious installers run the genuine program to avoid suspicion while secretly downloading a Python-based remote access trojan (RAT) from an external server. The RAT supports shell and Python command execution, file transfer, screen capture, and system information collection, and it checks for installed security products such as AhnLab V3 and CrowdStrike Falcon. Users of affected Q-Dir and DesktopOK versions should compare file hashes against the published values and check for RAT traces, since reinstalling the program may not remove the RAT. Software vendors should verify published hashes against delivered files and monitor for unauthorized changes to distributed binaries.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
